# {{lb|en|sports}} The [[spin]] or [[twist]] imparted to a [[ball]] etc. by a drawing stroke.
# {{lb|en|golf}} A [[golf]] shot that (for the right-handed player) curves intentionally to the left. See [[hook]], [[slice]], [[fade]].
# {{lb|en|curling}} A shot that is intended to land gently in the house (the circular target) without knocking out other stones; cf. ''[[takeout]]''.
# {{senseid|en|dry stream bed}} {{lb|en|geography}} A dry [[stream]] bed that drains surface water only during periods of heavy [[rain]] or [[flooding]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1918|author={{w|Willa Cather}}|title={{w|My Ántonia}}|publisher=Mirado Modern Classics|edition=paperback|page=15
|passage=The garden, curiously enough, was a quarter of a mile from the house, and the way to it led up a shallow '''draw''' past the cattle corral.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|countable}} A [[bag]] of [[cannabis]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Yvonne Ellis|title=Daughter, Arise: A Journey from Devastation to Restoration|page=54
|passage=So my friends and I would all chip in money to get a bag of weed or a '''draw'''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|uncountable}} Cannabis.
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2003|artist=w:Goldie Looking Chain|album=The Manifesto|title=Soap Bar|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EtVZbQkvk_Q|passage=Selling '''draw''' to your mates but it's really Oxo cubes.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|author=Michael Coleman|title=Old Skool Rave|page=139
|passage=Mick spoke to Simon, who was more of a drinker. He said that people who smoked '''draw''' were boring.}}
# {{lb|en|poker}} A situation in which one or more players has four cards of the same suit or four out of five necessary cards for a [[straight]] and requires a further card to make their [[flush]] or straight.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Ryan Wiseman|page=82|title=Earn $30,000 Per Month Playing Online Poker: A Step-By-Step Guide to Single|passage=The player to your left immediately raises you the minimum by clicking the raise button. This action immediately suggests that he's on a '''draw'''}}
# {{lb|en|horse racing}} The [[stall]] from which a [[horse]] [[begin]]s the [[race]].

